From e9d1b2a774615e2c0276f37eafcdf0b7fa0de818 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:05:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/43] pvr: teach the winsys submit paths timeline syncobjs
 (step 3, behaviour-preserving)

This was the real blocker for the sync-churn work. The queue could not hand a timeline syncobj
to the powervr winsys because the three submit paths could not express one:

  pvr_drm_job_render.c    5x assert(!(... VK_SYNC_IS_TIMELINE)), 5x HANDLE_TYPE_SYNCOBJ, .value = 0
  pvr_drm_job_compute.c   2x, 2x, 2x
  pvr_drm_job_transfer.c  2x, 2x, 2x

The asserts are compiled out in a release build, so migrating any job type in the queue submitted
its timeline sync as a binary syncobj at point 0 while the queue's timeline points advanced
independently: ordering lost, glmark2 segfaulted. Verified by doing exactly that and reverting.

Now one helper in pvr_drm_job_common.h picks the handle type from the sync itself:

  pvr_drm_sync_op_init(op, sync, flags, value)
    binary   -> DRM_PVR_SYNC_OP_FLAG_HANDLE_TYPE_SYNCOBJ,          .value = 0
    timeline -> DRM_PVR_SYNC_OP_FLAG_HANDLE_TYPE_TIMELINE_SYNCOBJ, .value = value

and all 9 asserts are gone. The two remaining HANDLE_TYPE_SYNCOBJ sites in the render path are the
driver's own internal geom_to_pr_syncobj, which is genuinely binary, so they stay as they are.

The flag exists in the UAPI (pvr_drm.h:1058, value 1) and pvr_drm_job_null.c already implemented
this correctly, so the pattern is copied from in-tree code rather than guessed.

Behaviour-preserving: every queue sync is still binary and every value still 0, so the helper
selects the same flag and value as before. This commit is what makes the next one (migrating job
types one at a time) safe to attempt.

Verified: build clean; bda, vk13, pctest, vk16, wgsize, samplers, storageimages, mrt, varyings,
inatt, ubos, stgbuf, vattrib all PASS; glmark2 --validate 27/0; glmark2 score 84.
